Vulkan: cap the usable API minor version at what the instance supports.

DeviceVK::Create takes m_MinorVersion from VkPhysicalDeviceProperties alone. CreateInstance asks
for min(vkEnumerateInstanceVersion, 1.4), so with an older loader in front of a newer driver
(Ubuntu 24.04's stock loader is 1.3.275; Mesa 25's lavapipe reports 1.4) the instance is 1.3 and
the device is treated as 1.4. Two things follow: ResolveDispatchTable loads the core 1.4 names
(vkCmdPushConstants2 and the other maintenance6 entry points) which the driver refuses to return
for a 1.3 instance, so CmdSetRootConstants calls a null pointer; and extensions that are only
core in 1.4 (VK_EXT_host_image_copy) are not enabled, so the validation layer rejects
VK_IMAGE_USAGE_HOST_TRANSFER_BIT. Both measured on v190 under WSL2 Ubuntu 24.04 with lavapipe
(docs/findings.md 8.4); both disappear with a 1.4 loader on LD_LIBRARY_PATH, or with this patch.

The patch clamps m_MinorVersion to the version CreateInstance requested. The wrapper path keeps
the caller's minorVersion. Applies on top of NRI v190 with patches 0001 to 0003.

diff --git a/Source/VK/DeviceVK.hpp b/Source/VK/DeviceVK.hpp
index a29ced9..cc92d62 100644
--- a/Source/VK/DeviceVK.hpp
+++ b/Source/VK/DeviceVK.hpp
@@ -802,6 +802,20 @@ Result DeviceVK::Create(const DeviceCreationDesc& desc, const DeviceCreationVKDe
                 NRI_REPORT_WARNING(this, "The device group does not support memory allocation on a subset of the physical devices");
 
             m_PhysicalDevice = deviceGroups[i].physicalDevices[0];
+
+            // PrismNRI patch 0004: the API version an application may use is the lower of the instance's and the
+            // physical device's. With an older loader in front of a newer driver (Ubuntu 24.04 ships a 1.3 loader,
+            // Mesa 25 reports 1.4) the device's minor version alone makes NRI request core 1.4 entry points the
+            // driver refuses for a 1.3 instance (CmdPushConstants2 comes back null and CmdSetRootConstants calls
+            // it) and skip extensions that are only core in 1.4 (VK_EXT_host_image_copy).
+            {
+                PFN_vkEnumerateInstanceVersion vkEnumerateInstanceVersion = (PFN_vkEnumerateInstanceVersion)m_VK.GetInstanceProcAddr(VK_NULL_HANDLE, "vkEnumerateInstanceVersion");
+                uint32_t instanceVersion = VK_API_VERSION_1_0;
+                if (vkEnumerateInstanceVersion && vkEnumerateInstanceVersion(&instanceVersion) == VK_SUCCESS) {
+                    uint32_t usableVersion = std::clamp(instanceVersion, VK_API_VERSION_1_2, VK_API_VERSION_1_4); // what CreateInstance asked for
+                    m_MinorVersion = std::min(m_MinorVersion, VK_API_VERSION_MINOR(usableVersion));
+                }
+            }
         }
     }
 
